FEATURE: message-box-module
DATE: 2026-10-09
SCOPE: new MessageBox notification module, built on the core slide utility

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AFFECTED PROJECTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Only the vUX library is changed. The change is additive: a new module, plus one
line in the module registry. Consumers (vGet, sketch-app, app.myinvitees.com) are
unaffected unless they import vUX-messageBox.js.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT CHANGED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

new MessageBox(); config; initialize(); then show(content, options) or
info/success/warning/error(). Effects: drop (default, from the top), slideLeft,
slideRight, fade, none. Alignment: left/center/right. duration (0 = sticky),
speed, type, theme, width, offset, maxVisible, closeButton, pauseOnHover,
closeOnClick, showProgress, newestOnTop, respectReducedMotion, onShow, onClose
(with a reason). show() returns a handle with close(), element and state.
CLAUDE.md gains the rule that new modules use the core and that reusable manual
operations are reported to the user.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
VERIFICATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Headless Chromium (playwright-core over the cached chrome-headless-shell),
1200x800, per-frame sampling:
  - drop/right: top -70 -> 16, out to -121; slideLeft/center: x 1224 -> 420, out
    to 1425; slideRight/left: x -384 -> 16, out to -484; fade: opacity 0 -> 1 -> 0;
    none: instant. onShow then onClose:timeout for each; the lane is removed when empty
  - stacking: three messages at 16/76/136; maxVisible 2 closed the two oldest with
    reason overflow
  - hover pause kept a 800ms message open for 1.5s; it closed after the pointer left
  - close during entry deferred until landing (reason api, no onShow); close
    button -> reason button
  - every validation error thrown with its message
  - a leaving message rises behind the one above it (screenshot)
  - example page at 1280 and 390 wide: no horizontal scroll, no console errors;
    Save (sticky + handle.close) and Undo (element content) work

dist/ (minified build) was not regenerated; run ./minify.sh to refresh it.
